REMARK     600
REMARK     600 THE LIGAND 3QZ IN THE STRUCTURE IS 17-HYDROXYPROGESTERONE,
REMARK     WHICH IS
REMARK     600 VERY HYDROPHOBIC AND ITS SOLUBILITY IS POOR. THE AUTHORS COULD
REMARK     NOT
REMARK     600 ADD MORE LIGAND DURING CRYSTALLIZATION DUE TO THE POOR
REMARK     SOLUBILITY.
REMARK     600 THIS IS PROBABLY WHY THE LIGANDS (ESPECIALLY B502) SHOWED
REMARK     600 RELATIVELY HIGH REAL SPACE R VALUES. THE DISORDER IS ALSO ONE
REMARK     OF
REMARK     600 THE REASON TO BE CONSIDERED. THERE ARE FOUR MOLECULES IN
REMARK     ASYMMETRIC
REMARK     600 UNIT. THREE OF FOUR MOLECULES A, C, AND D CLEARLY SHOWED TWO
REMARK     600 MOLECULES IN THE ENZYME. MOLECULE B SHOWED TWO MOLECULES AS
REMARK     WELL
REMARK     600 EVEN THOUGH B502 IS MORE DISORDERED SOMEHOW. IN ADDITION, THE
REMARK     600 BIOCHEMICAL TITRATION DATA PROVIDE ADDITIONAL EVIDENCE TO
REMARK     SUPPORT
REMARK     600 TWO LIGANDS BOUND IN THE ENZYME AT SAME TIME
